464	// Supports both committed checkpoints (by checkpoint ID) and temporary checkpoints (by git SHA).
465	// First tries to match committed checkpoints, then falls back to temporary checkpoints.
466	// When generate is true, generates an AI summary for the checkpoint.
467	// When force is true, regenerates even if a summary already exists.
468	// When rawTranscript is true, outputs only the raw transcript file (JSONL format).
469	// When searchAll is true, searches all commits without branch/depth limits (used for finding associated commits).
